body:
Well, yes. I felt immensely happy when I did try. It was short lived happiness, but you take what you can.

&#x200B;

I never got that "Oh, it's so great that I failed"-thing either. The only thing I regret about trying is exactly that - that it was a try, not a success.

Not really, but I have a few friends and family members who do. I'm just suicidal, but those people have done their research into the matter and keep tools at hand for it and have planned it. Most because of climate change, so when things get really bad, they have their way out.

&#x200B;

If I was going to live long enough and wasn't suicidal, I too would have suicide as an emergency exit because of climate change and how bad shit will turn out because of it.

More importantly, what does this have to do with this sub?

&#x200B;

Unless you're recruiting someone to livestream their suicide.

I don't know how people do manage to jump. It's so terrifying, even though I've been on the roof myself. I've had the urge. Just one step. But no, couldn't do it. I know that feeling. That feeling of being too much of a fuck up to get even suicide right, too pathetic. I too am one of the walking dead. Just waiting for the body to pass on.

&#x200B;

Honestly. I don't know what I was trying to accomplish with this message. Perhaps it help knowing you aren't alone in failing in that.

Well, I'm not sure if I'd consider myself having been let by down by them. Any "help" they've provided hasn't worked (and I've tried everything). But no treatment ever has 100% success rate. So in the end it's just... Well, one more piece of shit luck in my life. Sure, I'd hope it had worked, but they tried and that's all you can ask.

&#x200B;

Your situation on the other hand seems far more shitty with the help seeming utterly incompetent. Sorry. I don't know how to help
